# === Docker layer scanning false positives ===
#
# Root cause: python:3.11-slim base image ships wheel==0.45.1 and
# jaraco.context (via keyring dependency chain) in the system Python.
# Our Dockerfile upgrades these in a later layer, but Trivy scans ALL
# layers and finds the old METADATA files from the base image layer.
#
# Verified: `docker run --entrypoint sh <image> -c 'pip list | grep wheel'`
# shows 0.46.3 (upgraded), and the uv venv has jaraco.context==6.1.1.
# The vulnerable versions are shadowed and not reachable at runtime.
#
# To fully eliminate: switch to a base image without pip/wheel pre-installed,
# or use Docker BuildKit --squash to flatten layers.

# jaraco.context: base image has 5.3.0, our venv has 6.1.1 (pinned in pyproject.toml)
CVE-2026-23949

# wheel: base image has 0.45.1, our pip install upgrades to >=0.46.2
CVE-2026-24049
